   "tag": "C",
   "title": "One right-angled triangle",
   "stem": "From the top $T$ of a control tower $32$ m high, the angle of depression of an aircraft $A$ standing on the runway is $9^{\\circ}$. Find the distance of the aircraft from the foot of the tower.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "text": "The depression at the top equals the elevation at the aircraft, and carried down there it becomes an angle of the right-angled triangle."
    },
    {
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "\\tan 9^{\\circ} &= \\frac{32}{d}"
      },
      {
       "tex": "d &= \\frac{32}{\\tan 9^{\\circ}}"
      },
      {
       "tex": "d &= \\bl{202 \\text{ m}}"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "text": "GDC (Deg): $32 \\div \\tan 9$ → $202.04\\ldots$; write $d = 202$ m."
    }
   ],
