  {
   "type": "example",
   "n": 4,
   "tag": "C",
   "title": "Two elevations of the same point",
   "stem": "From a point $A$ on level ground the angle of elevation of the top $T$ of a chimney is $18^{\\circ}$. From a point $B$, which is $55$ m nearer the chimney on the same straight line, the angle of elevation is $29^{\\circ}$. Find the height of the chimney.",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "text": "The $55$ m is not a side of any right-angled triangle here, so the right triangle $TFB$ cannot be started. Work in triangle $ABT$ instead, where the $55$ m is a side. Its angle at $B$ is the supplement of $29^{\\circ}$, because that angle is on the other side of $B$."
    },
    {
     "steps": [
      {
       "tex": "A\\hat{B}T &= 180^{\\circ} - 29^{\\circ} = 151^{\\circ}"
      },
      {
       "tex": "A\\hat{T}B &= 180^{\\circ} - 18^{\\circ} - 151^{\\circ} = 11^{\\circ}"
      }
     ]
    }
   ],
